; Go APIs may expose result validity through a paired result, such as an error,
; or directly through a nullable result. The language alone does not establish
; either contract.
; This rule starts from reviewed semantic-model contracts. Its conservative
; built-in scope covers selected os file APIs through the embedded
; bifrost.go.stdlib.os pack, plus net.Dial, net.DialTimeout, and net.Listen
; through the embedded bifrost.go.stdlib.net pack, and encoding/pem.Decode
; through the embedded bifrost.go.stdlib.encoding-pem pack.
;
; Candidate discovery and proof are identity-based throughout. The structural
; seed limits work to modeled member names, then `result-contract-calls` keeps
; only calls whose canonical dispatch identity positively selects an activated
; result contract. Import aliases therefore work without admitting unrelated
; local methods with the same name. The contract relation maps the protected
; result and any separate condition result through procedure-local assignment
; events and guard facts. The explicit `result-contract-operation-uses`
; relation projects each intrinsic or member operation with reviewed
; applicability and its exact guard verdict. The policy therefore selects
; assignment-form calls inside a callable without crossing a nested callable
; to find that assignment:
; tuple forwarding, callback-local forwarding, and package initializers are
; outside this intraprocedural use-before-check claim and must not make an
; absence claim globally incomplete.
; Only an operation whose complete reviewed contract requires the protected
; receiver, or an intrinsic dereference/field/index operation, can match.
; Unreviewed and ambiguous operations remain open and never become findings.
; Plain propagation is deliberately not proof of misuse because the receiving
; API may accept the zero value.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.go-result-used-before-success-check"
  :name "Go result used before its success condition"
  :message "this operation requires a valid Go API result on a path where its reviewed success condition has not been proved"
  :severity error
  :description "A reviewed API contract says this operation requires a valid result, but no modeled success condition for that exact result has been proved at the operation. Success may be established by a predicate on a paired result, such as an error being nil, or directly on the protected result, such as a nullable pointer being non-nil. Nil-tolerant methods, unreviewed members, and plain value propagation are not findings."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "go" "error-handling" "nil"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name use
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (language go
          (result-contract-operation-uses
            (call-result-contracts
              (result-contract-calls
                (call-shape
                  (inside (callable)
                    (inside-decl (assignment)
                      (call :callee (name/regex "^(Open|OpenFile|Create|CreateTemp|Stat|Lstat|Dial|DialTimeout|Listen|Decode)$")
                            :receiver (identifier)))))))))))
    (filter :over use
      :where ((use.applicability eq required)
              (use.guard eq unguarded)))
    (group :name by-acquisition :by (use.acquisition_id)
      (aggregate :name violations :op count))
    (assert :group by-acquisition :value violations :cardinality (exactly 0))))
